el ~1.0x), GateUp 80/80 (even layer0\\n        # 113k exc wins 1.31x -- its 940MB avoided write swamps exceptions), Down\\n        # 80/80.  We accept the 1-2 extreme-outlier layers (e.g. QKV layer0)\\n        # being slower rather than gate per layer -- aggregate TPOT cost ~0.1%.\\n        # (Earlier QKV=0 was a layer-0 sampling artifact: the isolated bench's\\n        # real-weight loader only ever sees layer 0, the 314k outlier.  Most QKV\\n        # layers have ~1.6k exceptions and fuse-win.)\\n        # best-N re-derived by an 8-step N sweep on a representative (median-exc)\\n        # real layer (layer 40, N=8..256, H2D).  Cliff is structural: at N>64 the\\n        # small-M shapes (QKV/O/Down) remap to the slow Npad=192 WGMMA tile\\n        # (_pad_n), so they lose past 64; GateUp's large M keeps a clean Npad=128\\n        # and keeps winning to 128.  Ratios @best-N: QKV 1.12x, O 1.09x, GateUp\\n        # 1.20x@128, Down 1.49x.\\n        (10240, 8192): 64,    # QKV    (wins N<=64 ~1.12x; N>=96 -> Npad=192 cliff)\\n        (8192, 8192): 128,    # O      (serving batch-128: avoid dense WDecomp)\\n        (57344, 8192): 128,   # GateUp (was 64; wins to 128, big M -> Npad=128)\\n        (8192, 28672): 128,   # Down   (serving batch-128: avoid dense WDecomp)\\n    }\\n\\n    def _fused_max_n_for(self, M: int, K: int) -> int:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Per-layer fused N threshold (0 = never fuse this shape); unknown\\n        shapes fall back to 128.  An instance-level ``_fused_max_n_override``\\n        (set by tests/benchmarks) overrides all shapes.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self._fused_max_n_override is not None:\\n            return self._fused_max_n_override\\n        return self._FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE.get((M, K), 128)\\n\\n    def linear_apply(self, comp, x, wdecomp_events=None):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Fused decode + GEMM forward: y = x @ W^T, x [..., K] -> [..., M].\\n\\n        Uses the P4-RS register-A WGMMA kernel for decode-N (N <=\\n        ``_fused_max