{"timestamp":"2026-08-27T09:49:38.435Z","ordinal":1374,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a042a0-0503-7a71-ad7b-f49743bb72d8","call_id":"call_STKmgmfNKOZmwcWvasX2ThHQ","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"NVIDIA GH200 480GB, 97871 MiB\nusage: fuseGEMM.py [-h] [--codecs CODECS] [--projs PROJS]\n                   [--n-values N_VALUES] [--tp TP] [--synthetic]\n                   [--weights-dir WEIGHTS_DIR] [--shards SHARDS]\n                   [--layers LAYERS] [--layer LAYER] [--repeat-id REPEAT_ID]\n                   [--seed SEED] [--warmup WARMUP] [--iters ITERS]\n                   [--no-flush] [--no-h2d] [--h2d-bytes H2D_BYTES] [--check]\n                   [--no-validate] [--full-model] [--ats]\n                   [--ats-pool-gib ATS_POOL_GIB]\n                   [--ats-hugepage-dir ATS_HUGEPAGE_DIR]\n                   [--ats-lpddr-node ATS_LPDDR_NODE] --csv CSV\n\nUnified codec decision benchmark for the tiered-serving weight path.\n\nFor each compressor codec (zipserv / p4flat / ublb_flat / chunk_delta3) and each Llama-3.1-70B\nprojection (qkv, o, gate_up, down) this measures the data needed to calibrate\nthe serving strategy, per token count N, between three choices:\n\n  1. fused             — decompress + GEMM in one kernel (no dense HBM write)\n  2. decomp-then-GEMM  — decompress to a dense bf16 weight, then cuBLAS\n  3. raw bf16 load     — skip compression, GEMM the dense bf16 weight directly\n                         (the compute floor; its load cost = raw_bytes / BW is\n                         estimated from the reported ratio)\n\nReported per (codec, proj):\n  * compress time, decompress time, compression ratio + compressed bytes\nReported per (codec, layer, proj, N), under TWO conditions — isolated and with a\nconcurrent H2D memcpy running (mimicking the next layer's weight offload):\n  * raw GEMM, decomp+GEMM, fused latency P50/P95\n\nWhy the concurrent-H2D condition: decomp-then-GEMM writes the full dense weight\nto HBM, which contends with the weight-offload H2D copy + HBM write bandwidth;\nfused has no dense write and is contention-immune. An isolated sweep therefore\nwrongly favours decomp for O/GateUp/Down — the in-engine flip the codec\nthreshold tables (P4FlatCompressor._FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE etc.) already encode.\n\nTo characterise the fused KERNEL at every N (so production thresholds can be\ncalibrated), the per-codec production N-thresholds are forced wide open.\n\nUsage:\n  PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) ./.venv/bin/python benchmark_codec_decision.py\n  ... --synthetic --check --n-values 1,64,256\n  ... --csv codec_decision.csv\n  ... --codecs zipserv,p4flat --projs o,gate_up\n  ... --ats --codecs p4flat --projs gate_up   # GH200: exp->LPDDR/C2C, mant->HBM\n\nWith ``--ats`` (GH200 only) the codec's compressed-exponent stream is relocated\nto Grace LPDDR (the raw sign|mantissa byte stream stays in HBM) and BOTH\ncompressed strategies are re-measured reading that exponent over the NVLink-C2C\nlink, adding two iso/h2d column groups:\n\n  * decmpATS  — decompress (exponent from LPDDR/C2C, mantissa from HBM) into a\n                dense bf16 weight in HBM, then cuBLAS GEMM (still an HBM write).\n  * fusedATS  — fused decode+GEMM; the exponent streams from LPDDR straight into\n                the SMs, no dense-weight HBM staging at all.\n\nThis gives the direct HBM-vs-C2C comparison for the decomp+GEMM and fused paths\nalike.  See\n``ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py``.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --codecs CODECS\n  --projs PROJS\n  --n-values N_VALUES\n  --tp TP               tensor-parallel degree (shards shapes; needs\n                        --synthetic for tp>1)\n  --synthetic           random bf16 weights instead of the real checkpoint\n  --weights-dir WEIGHTS_DIR\n  --shards SHARDS       max safetensor shards to scan for real weights\n  --layers LAYERS       comma-separated real checkpoint layers; official\n                        scaling run uses the outlier-heavy 0 and\n                        representative 40\n  --layer LAYER         legacy single-layer override for --layers\n  --repeat-id REPEAT_ID\n                        independent-process repeat recorded in every CSV row\n  --seed SEED           base seed for reproducible BF16 activations\n  --warmup WARMUP\n  --iters ITERS\n  --no-flush            disable L2 flush between iters\n  --no-h2d              skip the concurrent-H2D contention condition\n  --h2d-bytes H2D_BYTES\n                        H2D contention traffic per copy (0 = codec compressed\n                        size)\n  --check               print per-row fused OK/INVALID marker (validity gate\n                        is always on unless --no-validate)\n  --no-validate         skip the fused bit-exactness gate (trust fused\n                        timings)\n  --full-model          print per-layer / full-model strategy totals\n  --ats                 also measure the fused GEMM with the compressed\n                        exponent in Grace LPDDR (mantissa in HBM), read by the\n                        SMs over NVLink-C2C/ATS (no HBM staging). GH200 only.\n                        Adds 'fusedATS' columns.\n  --ats-pool-gib ATS_POOL_GIB\n                        LPDDR ATS pool size per projection (GiB)\n  --ats-hugepage-dir ATS_HUGEPAGE_DIR\n                        hugetlbfs mount for the ATS pool; falls back to\n                        numa_alloc_onnode if no free hugepages\n  --ats-lpddr-node ATS_LPDDR_NODE\n                        NUMA node for the LPDDR fallback (Grace = 0 on GH200)\n  --csv CSV             output CSV; required so official cells cannot be lost\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04299-2157-7bc2-8905-294a069ebf98","create_time":1787824178.4355323}}}
